## Result summary

**Deliverable:** `/work/submission.csv` — 296,302 rows, columns `id,addicted_label`, ids identical to `/data/sample_submission.csv` in the same order, all predicted probabilities in [0,1] (min 0.0001, max ~1.0, mean 0.7095 ≈ train base rate). All format checks PASS.

**Modeling:**
- Binary target (~71% positive), heavy missingness (up to ~19% in screen-time cols). LightGBM handles missing numerics natively and treats categorical NaN as its own category — no risky imputation/encoding pipeline.
- Baseline plain LightGBM, 5-fold stratified CV ROC AUC: **0.9636**.
- Optuna TPE tuning (25 trials, 200k-row stratified subsample, 3-fold) + feature engineering (screen-time ratios, notif-per-app-open, screen-per-awake-hour, age², etc.).
- Chosen config verified on full 5-fold CV: **0.9646 ± 0.0005** (oof 0.9646), refit on all 691,369 training rows to produce test predictions.
- Runtime ~45 min of the 60-min budget.

**Note:** `/work/.harness` is owned by uid 1001 and not writable by this session (uid 1000), so harness state lives in `/work/.harness-state/` (intent.md, world.md, decisions.md, evidence.md, aar.md, plus scripts/metrics). Only `/work/submission.csv` counts for the deliverable.

Evidence of every acceptance criterion is logged in `/work/.harness-state/evidence.md`. No public leaderboard score is available (no internet), so performance is evidenced solely by local CV.
